  "notes": "The palette looks like a Material 3 tonal scheme (teal primary #006a6a, neutral surfaces #f2f5f4/#ecefee, outline #6f7979). Buttons are full pill shapes (9999px): Save and Invite are filled teal, while the rest are teal text-only, and Delete is outlined with a subtle shadow. Inputs have 4px corners, selects 8px, the main panel 12px, and member rows 8px. The page is plain and unstyled in places: the activity log is a raw browser bulleted list (disc and circle markers) that runs about 2,600px with no pagination or filtering, and it shows HTML-escaped '&gt;' in the content. The copy is plain-language and self-explanatory ('Who may do what', 'Hand over the group', 'Whatever the group allows', 'An invitation reaches an address rather than an account...'). Per-member 'Can' selects override the group-level policy. Deleting asks for confirmation in an inline pink strip, not a modal. The header icon nav has no visible text labels."
